    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_321f7935645b3ae683125e6c2fa4c0916c169c788d2efc303cf1805a0e82c3fa",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In mean-square and trace-formula approaches, crossing beyond diagonal control turns zero pair correlation into an off-diagonal problem involving shifted products Lambda(n)Lambda(n+h). Encoding prime powers by the von Mangoldt function isolates that statistic; a transition-range calculation then treats diagonal Lambda(n)^2 sums under RH separately from off-diagonal singular-series terms supplied by a Twin Prime hypothesis.",
