    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3bbb386419cc9b9b20de3cd3230b1d3eeca9aeb23baf6b66dd59791e0ff71c2d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For finitely many nearby log-zeta evaluations, the limiting capped-minimum covariance admits an exact Gaussian ancestor-tree realization by shared independent increments. Extreme-value and free-energy proofs use a parallel multiscale geometry operationally: prime blocks are variance-matched, close grid points share early scales, small-prime trunks are removed when the window changes, and second-moment or entropy-amplitude arguments count simultaneous high paths across blocks.",
