      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3f9eda4df32ac988bb8ce77923255a38a97ed428fe2460b1fdb27930f785fc37",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Littlewood- or Jensen-type reductions replace a zero-location question by a mollified mean square of an auxiliary differential combination. Once a mean-value theorem expresses that square in terms of admissible coefficient profiles, improving an aggregate zero proportion becomes constrained optimization: a quadratic functional with an Euler-Lagrange boundary problem, a six-component diagonal/cross-term scalar objective for a three-piece mollifier, or a polynomial approximation to a relaxed sinh profile for high derivative order.",
