    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_43ffe7f0d1959c5d6238a898a1ceb213fd0a7d8491aaced0376ae4f1fb0c2a01",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Lengthening a Dirichlet polynomial past the diagonal range exposes additional off-diagonal terms rather than merely improving an approximation. In the moment recipe, polynomial length selects the maximum swap cardinality that survives Perron contour movement; in the divisor-correlation program, strata with a specified number of nonzero discrepancies reproduce the corresponding swap grades after partition multiplicities are included.",
