    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4866e317b48a744d2ac0cfdacfe3ce8a7f6850b823387c7d8f64477f80396dbe",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The dimensionless separation is physical displacement times local spectral density. For two shifted values, that scale distinguishes coalescing, finite-correlation, and separated leading regimes, with coalescing unitary poles recovering one characteristic-polynomial moment of combined weight. For an observation conditioned at an eigenvalue, a separate spherical-Bessel factor describes the crossover from zero-offset derivative behavior toward ordinary field-moment scaling as the density-scaled displacement grows.",
