      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Several moment programs encode candidate main terms by polar data. A multiplicative diagonal equality produces pairwise zeta factors and a regular Euler product carrying local arithmetic; matching singular parts in shifted-divisor coordinates yields a residue identity and local coefficient bounds; adding a discriminant variable turns a quadratic-family mean into the prospective w=1 residue of a corrected multiple Dirichlet series.",
