      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Matching matrix dimension to local mean zero density selects a finite-N characteristic-polynomial comparison at finite zeta height. Structured non-Gaussian log-value deviations and slowly converging low-zero or local-maximum statistics can therefore coexist with an asymptotic unitary model, but only as calibrated finite-height evidence rather than as proof or a universal excuse for discrepancies.",
